---
// Prose against the manifest, not three orphan cards: the claims on the left
// are answered by the image's own readout on the right.
import Manifest from './Manifest.astro';
---

<div class="inside">
  {/* A ruled list, the site's house container: each row names what the thing
      does for you, then how. The manifest beside it is the proof. */}
  <dl class="facts">
    <div class="fact">
      <dt>Games run as they should</dt>
      <dd>
        Gamescope, GameMode and MangoHud are built in. ntsync is there for Proton, split-lock
        mitigation is off and the memory-map limit is raised, because games want all three.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="fact">
      <dt>A bad update undoes itself</dt>
      <dd>
        Every boot is health-checked. If the desktop fails to come up three times running, the
        machine goes back to the previous version without being&nbsp;asked.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="fact">
      <dt>Scheduling for hybrid CPUs</dt>
      <dd>
        <code>scx_bpfland</code> places threads across performance and efficiency cores where the
        kernel can load it. Where it cannot, the stock scheduler runs instead of nothing; the
        manifest's <code>scheduler_btf</code> line says which this build&nbsp;got.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="fact">
      <dt>Ready for work</dt>
      <dd>
        distrobox for any Linux userland, libvirt/KVM for virtual machines. Apps are Flatpaks, with
        Flathub unfiltered; <span class="ns">the image is the&nbsp;OS.</span>
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="fact">
      <dt>NVIDIA with Secure Boot on</dt>
      <dd>
        The open NVIDIA driver is built for the image's exact kernel and signed, so Secure Boot
        stays&nbsp;on.
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
  <Manifest />
</div>

<style>
  .inside {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 6fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .facts {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 58ch;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .fact {
    padding: var(--space-md) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .fact:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-display-weight);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    line-height: var(--heading-lh);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .inside {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
